Corrected message:

Stop re-adding add-in icon search paths for every node at startup

The icon search-path rescan ran for each extension node, including the
batch reported for already-installed add-ins at startup. The startup
scan had already run, and adding a search path does not de-duplicate,
so each add-in's path piled up once per node. It now rescans only for
add-ins installed while the app is running.

Also:
- Resize Palette returns the reset confirmation's answer directly; the
  palette helper that wrapped it (its first argument was always false)
  and its tests are removed.
- The deferred-action scheduler override is no longer public.
